  "problem_context": {
    "problem_statement": "Reverify the real CRTOS CircularAreaRead and its internal query/helper call chain after adopting the idmanager-style circular_area_state/store_circular_area resource. Remove CircularAreaBackingResource and all caller-visible ring representation witnesses from public and internal API contracts. The public Read contract must expose only the abstract circular state plus the caller-owned output-buffer state needed to describe bytes written.",
    "target_function": "CircularAreaRead",
    "expected_behavior": "On invalid output/null/zero-length or empty FIFO, return ERROR and preserve the circular state and any owned output buffer. On success, actual=min(requested,Zlength(ca_contents state)); copy the FIFO prefix into output[0..actual), drop that prefix from ca_contents, preserve capacity and all hidden backing/descriptor resources, set the hidden read index consistently and status to zero, and return EOK. Preserve exact CRTOS memcpy/wrap behavior and original function body.",
    "input_output_contract": "Use store_circular_area state circular_area as the sole circular-area ownership at every public/internal call boundary. Define pure Read result/transition relations over circular_area_state and output contents in the case lib as needed. Output capacity/physical contents are legitimate caller-owned resources, but data_buffer/readidx/writeidx/status/operations/physical ring bytes must remain hidden inside store_circular_area. Init and Reset outputs must call Read without representation conversion.",
    "spec_hint": [
      "Use one abstract state binder for the circular area. It is acceptable to bind output_capacity/output_before because they describe a separate caller buffer. Update the embedded CircularAreaIsFull/IsEmpty/GetDataLength/DivideRdData specs and callsite where clauses to consume and return the same store_circular_area state. Open the representation only with internal full Assert points required for field access/memcpy, following the Reset pattern. Do not weaken memcpy byte semantics and do not switch mixed_full to full."
    ],
